Now add endpoints before `return server;`. Also need a helper `persistAcceptedSuggestion` maybe inline.

Accept flow:
```
server.post<{ Params:{suggestionId:string}; Body: AcceptSuggestionBody }>('/api/v1/suggestions/:suggestionId/accept', async (request, reply) => {
  const suggestion = await suggestionRepo.findById(...)
  if (!suggestion || suggestion.isDeleted) 404
  if (suggestion.status !== 'pending') 409
  const body = request.body ?? {};
  const now = body.now ? new Date(body.now) : new Date();
  if (Number.isNaN(now.getTime())) 400
  const eventId = body.eventId ?? `event-${randomUUID()}`;
  let dayId = body.dayId ?? suggestion.proposed.dayId ?? `day-${getLocalDateString(new Date(suggestion.proposed.startAt), 'UTC')}`;
  // accept might throw
  let accepted; let proposed;
  try { ({suggestion: accepted, proposed} = acceptSuggestion(suggestion, body.overrides, { eventId, dayId, now, source:'imported'})); } catch (err) { reply.code(400).send(...); return; }
  const event = buildEventFromSuggestion(proposed, {eventId, dayId, now, source:'imported'});
  // resolve tags/people
  const existingTags = await tagRepo.listTree(); ...
  const resolvedTags = resolveTagsForEvent(event.id, proposed.tagPaths ?? [], existingTags, {now});
  ...
  db.exec('BEGIN IMMEDIATE')
  try {
    event.dayId = await ensureDay(dayId, event.startAt);
    await eventRepo.save(event);
    for tags... save, assign
    for people... save, link
    await suggestionRepo.save(accepted);
    if (suggestion.source === 'calendar' && suggestion.externalId) {
      const item: CalendarItem = { eventId: event.id, externalId: suggestion.externalId, importedAt: now.toISOString(), attendees: [] };
      await calendarItemRepo.save(item);
    }
    db.exec('COMMIT')
  } catch ... rollback 500
  return { suggestion: accepted, event, tags, eventTags, people, participants };
});
```
Note: accepted uses reviewedAt now. But accepted.suggestion has acceptedEventId eventId. Good.

dayId in event may have been changed by ensureDay; accepted.proposed.dayId remains original maybe. Not critical.

Reject:
```
server.post('/api/v1/suggestions/:suggestionId/reject', ...) 
```
No body; now optional `now`.

Edit (PATCH):
```
const body = request.body ?? {};
const edited = editSuggestion(suggestion, body, now); await save; return edited;
```
Catches invalid input -> 400.

GET suggestions:
```
server.get<{ Querystring: { status?: string; includeDeleted?: string } }>('/api/v1/suggestions', ...)
```
Validate status among pending/accepted/rejected else 400. If no status -> listAll.

Extensions:
```
server.get('/api/v1/extensions', () => extensionRegistry.list());
```
Calendar import:
```
server.post<{ Body: CalendarImportBody }>('/api/v1/extensions/calendar/import', async (request, reply) => {
  const body = request.body;
  if (!body || typeof body.ics !== 'string') 400
  const parsed = parseIcsCalendar(body.ics);
  const candidate = calendarEventsToSuggestions(parsed.events);
  const created: Suggestion[] = [];
  const duplicates: Array<{externalId, suggestionId}> = [];
  for (const suggestion of candidate) {
    if (!suggestion.externalId) { ... }
    const existing = await suggestionRepo.findByExternalId('calendar', suggestion.externalId);
    if (existing) { duplicates.push(...); continue; }
    await suggestionRepo.save(suggestion);
    created.push(suggestion);
  }
  return { extension: CALENDAR_EXTENSION, importedCount: created.length, suggestions: created, duplicates, skipped: parsed.skipped };
});
```
Note calendarName: we're not storing until accept; could return it. CalendarItem on accept has no calendarName. Could extend suggestion notes? Simpler: ignore calendarName in import body; but maybe store in notes? We can pass calendarName to compose? Not necessary. But to be faithful module metadata, could attach calendarName to proposed.notes? Eh, accept can't know. Alternatively keep a map? We can include calendar name in notes prefix? Let's skip since body calendarName optional is unused; remove it from type to avoid unused. Actually unused interface field is harmless but lint? no lint. Keep but not use? Better remove to avoid confusion. I'll use it in the response only? No. Let's remove calendarName from CalendarImportBody. Actually could be useful to tag the imported item; but CalendarItem only saved on accept. We don't have storage of suggestion-specific calendar name other than notes. I'll leave it out.

Also extension GET returns registry list, which includes CALENDAR_EXTENSION. ExtensionRegistration imported for type? We imported it but may not use -> TS noUnusedLocals likely on. Let me check tsconfig. Root tsc may have noUnusedLocals. Existing imports like `Day` etc. used. If I import ExtensionRegistration but don't use, build fails. I'll use it in a helper or remove. Remove from imports for now. Also CALENDAR_EXTENSION used in import response. Good.

Let me write endpoints.

