content.text:
Now create SuggestionInbox.tsx. Need no emoji. Neutral palette consistent.

Props:
```
interface SuggestionInboxProps {
  suggestions: Suggestion[];
  isLoading: boolean;
  onAccept: (id: string) => Promise<void>;
  onReject: (id: string) => Promise<void>;
  onEdit: (id: string, overrides: SuggestionOverrides) => Promise<void>;
  onImportCalendar: (ics: string) => Promise<CalendarImportResult>;
}
```
State: editingId, form fields, busyId, error, importMessage, importing.

Rendering:
- section card.
- header row with title and import label input file.
- if no pending, empty text.
- suggestion rows: time block (start–end), body title, meta (source badge, confidence maybe "confidence 90%"), notes preview maybe first line.
- action buttons Accept (primary light), Edit (secondary), Reject (secondary).
- edit panel: inputs for title, start/end (datetime-local). Save / Cancel.
- import message line.

For datetime-local conversion: since ISO UTC, display local:
```
function toLocalInputValue(iso?: string): string {
  if (!iso) return '';
  const d = new Date(iso);
  if (Number.isNaN(d.getTime())) return '';
  const pad=(n)=>String(n).padStart(2,'0');
  return `${d.getFullYear()}-${pad(d.getMonth()+1)}-${pad(d.getDate())}T${pad(d.getHours())}:${pad(d.getMinutes())}`;
}
function fromLocalInputValue(value: string): string | undefined {
  if (!value) return undefined;
  const d = new Date(value);
  if (Number.isNaN(d.getTime())) return undefined;
  return d.toISOString();
}
```

When starting edit, set fields from suggestion. Save builds overrides:
- title trimmed; if no change? still send, fine.
- startAt = fromLocalInputValue(start) ?? original.
- endAt: if end empty -> null (clear); else iso. Include only if changed? Just include; if end empty, null.
- notes maybe not editable.
Call onEdit then clear state.

Accept button: directly onAccept. But if editing, maybe Accept uses saved edits only. Fine.

Timezone display format uses toLocaleTimeString.

File input onChange handler: read file via `await file.text()`, call onImportCalendar, set message:
`Imported ${result.importedCount} ${...}. ${result.duplicateCount} already known.` plus skipped count. If result 0 and duplicate 0: "No calendar events found."
catch setError.

Let's write.

